sequenceDiagram
    actor Caller
    participant X as Xor2
    participant NA as not_a:NAND
    participant NB as not_b:NAND
    participant AB as a_not_b:AND
    participant BA as not_a_b:AND
    participant O as combine:OR
    Note over Caller,O: Existing Xor2 has A=0, B=1, out=1. Change only A to 1.
    Caller->>X: setA(1)
    activate X
    X->>X: a = 1, then update()
    X->>NA: setIn1(1)
    NA->>NA: in1 = 1, then update()
    X->>NA: setIn2(1)
    NA->>NA: in2 = 1, then update() sets out=0
    X->>NB: setIn1(1)
    NB->>NB: in1 = 1, then update()
    X->>NB: setIn2(1)
    NB->>NB: in2 = 1, then update() sets out=0
    X->>AB: setIn1(a=1)
    AB->>AB: in1 = 1, then update()
    X->>NB: getOut()
    NB-->>X: 0
    X->>AB: setIn2(0)
    AB->>AB: in2 = 0, then update() sets out=0
    X->>NA: getOut()
    NA-->>X: 0
    X->>BA: setIn1(0)
    BA->>BA: in1 = 0, then update()
    X->>BA: setIn2(b=1)
    BA->>BA: in2 = 1, then update() sets out=0
    X->>AB: getOut()
    AB-->>X: 0
    X->>O: setIn1(0)
    O->>O: in1 = 0, then update()
    X->>BA: getOut()
    BA-->>X: 0
    X->>O: setIn2(0)
    O->>O: in2 = 0, then update() sets out=0
    X->>O: getOut()
    O-->>X: 0
    X->>X: out = 0
    X-->>Caller: setA returns after all outputs settle
    deactivate X
    Caller->>X: getOut()
    X-->>Caller: 0
    Note over X,O: Every primitive setter calls update, even for unchanged input values.
